# Documentation map

Entry point for all documentation. Rules for agents: [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md). Formats,
statuses, ownership of files, and lifecycle: [`documentation-rules.md`](documentation-rules.md).
One fact has one owner document; every other document links to it instead of repeating it.

## What exists and which document owns which facts

| Kind of fact | Owner document | State |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Product name and purpose; the repository settings the owner sets once | [`README.md`](../README.md) | exists |
| Agent rules: precedence, autonomy by risk, when a change is done, required checks | [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) | exists |
| Environment commands: set up, check, fast check, end-to-end tests, reset, the check after every edit | `scripts/env.sh` with `setup`, `check`, `fast`, `e2e`, or `reset`, which runs the commands of `.claude/harness.conf`: check is `scripts/check.sh`, fast check `scripts/check-docs.sh` until the project sets its own; setup, end-to-end tests, reset: not decided until the project sets them. `CHECK_EDIT` runs after every edit through `.claude/hooks/post-edit-check.sh`; not decided until the project sets it. The `afe-init` skill sets them up with the owner | check and fast check exist |
| Documentation statuses, lifecycle, path classes and access, ownership of files, alignment, review checklist | [`documentation-rules.md`](documentation-rules.md) | exists |
| Branches, commit messages, pull requests, template updates, review of pull requests | [`contributing.md`](contributing.md); applied in Claude Code by the skills `.claude/skills/create-pr/` and `.claude/skills/update-template/`{% if code_review %}, in CI by `.claude/skills/review-code/`{% endif %}{% if dual_review %}, before a pull request by `.claude/skills/dual-review/`{% endif %} | exists |
| What a test is for and must prove, gates on tests | [`testing-rules.md`](testing-rules.md) | exists |
| Why a costly-to-reverse decision was made, and its status | [`decisions/README.md`](decisions/README.md), the generated index of short ADRs; other owner decisions are marked in their owner documents ([`documentation-rules.md`](documentation-rules.md), sections 3 and 5) | exists; the index lists the records |
| Checks and enforcement | `scripts/check.sh` and the scripts it runs; Claude Code hooks and permissions `.claude/settings.json`, generated from `.claude/settings.project.json`, and `.claude/hooks/`; path classes `.claude/path-classes`; harness settings `.claude/harness.conf`; workflows `.github/workflows/`; metrics of merged pull requests `scripts/pr-metrics.sh` ([`documentation-rules.md`](documentation-rules.md), sections 7, 8, and 9) | exists |

## Planned sections

The documentation has a fixed set of sections ([`documentation-rules.md`](documentation-rules.md),
section 2). A planned section is created only when its first real content exists, through an
explicit change approved by the owner; this table is updated in the same change. Do not create
placeholder files.

| Kind of fact | Planned owner | Created when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Requirements: what the system must do | `docs/requirements/`, one `REQ-NNN` per statement | the owner states the first requirement |
| Invariants: what must hold everywhere, each with the check that enforces it | `docs/invariants.md`, one `INV-NN` per invariant | the owner names the first invariant |
| Architecture: the system map, components, domain ownership, boundaries and dependency rules, runtime | `docs/architecture/` | the first design is proposed |
| Contracts: APIs, schemas, events | `contracts/` at the repository root, machine-readable and authoritative | the first interface is designed |
| Active plans | `docs/plans/` | work spans more than one session |
| Operations: run, deploy, observe (logs, traces, metrics, scenario replay), recover | `docs/operations/` | there is something to operate |
| Conventions: the rules of one area that the code does not make obvious ([`documentation-rules.md`](documentation-rules.md), section 2) | `docs/conventions/`, one file per area | the first convention is agreed |
| Recipes: step-by-step procedures for repeated work, such as adding a module or an endpoint | `docs/recipes/`, one file per task; a skill or tool-specific rule file points to its recipe instead of copying it | a task is done the same way a second time |
| Implemented behaviour | source code and its tests | the first code is merged |
| Review criteria: what the project adds to the rubric of [`contributing.md`](contributing.md), section 6 | not decided: the owner document the project chooses | the project adds its first criterion |

## Reading order for a new agent

1. [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md)
2. This map
3. Only the documents the task needs, following links from here
